ze keys passes the limit with no key over it; the PDF case does not reach it (BUDGET-2024-APP's reading without its text units is 189,015 B, its text being in `capture_text` rows, :1206). *Memory:* the entries make a sheet's records and cells whole before anything is stored: `csv-reader/index.mjs:578` `walkRecords` holds every record (14.9 MB per MB of file) and :741-793 builds the whole `cells` list (72,392 objects of about 221 B for a 1 MB CSV, 16 MB per MB); `formats-xlsx.mjs:500-515` holds the shared strings as one list and :1008-1012 makes every `typedCell` of a sheet; so storing the cells in side rows alone would still die at the object's 128 MB (lowest surviving cap 133 at 1 MB, 178 at 2, 265 at 4, 433 at 8, against the real shape `128 + 39 - N` = 166, 165, 163, 159; only the streamed path, `csv-reader/index.mjs:545-555` and :741 `cells = parts.stream ? null : []`, holds, at 117 for 8 MB, and it drops the cells). Bob (K4630): a file within the standard's bound is read whole, never refused or left to fail. **The design (K4631 c1-c8; Option A of `diagnosis-R6-g41.md` section 2 as amended).** **c1 the row rule** (extraction): a stored reading row, `readings.reading` and every `reading_history.reading`, stays under 1 MiB: a top-level key over `READING_KEY_BYTES` is spilled, and then the largest remaining keys one by one until the row is under; spilled into `reading_parts` rows of at most 256 Ki characters, the key in the row replaced by the stub `{"$part": {"sha", "bytes", "n"}}`; never spilled: `found`, `failure`, `basis`, `tier3_candidate`, `text_container`, `page_count`, `at`, `text_source`, `entities` (spilled last of all and only if it alone holds the row over, its count then read from the row's `entity_count`, :1027, so no site needs the list; a lean accessor); the history's `provenance` column (:1134) is under the same rule; a stub is honoured only when extraction wrote it and its parts exist (a document's own `{"$part": ...}` in `facts` is data, and a stu